        <mxCell id="BTorxVMLyVCxX_XMpz2y-30" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="Data flow at each time step \(k\): \(S_k\;\to\;(O^{i}_{k},\, F^{i}_{\mathrm{DSS},k})\;\to\;U^{i}_{\mathrm{DSS},k}\;\subset\;F_{\mathrm{in},k}\;\to\;\Phi(\cdot)\;\to\;S_{k+1}\) [Equation (53)].&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br&gt;The DSS Core never writes to \(S_k(x,y)\) directly; all intervention effects propagate through the external input set \(F_{\mathrm{in},k}\), preserving the architectural separation established in Section 4.1." vertex="1">
